course: dictionary
lesson: 6543
title: Newborn: just born
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: New and born are two words you already know. Put them together and newborn means just born, only a few hours, days or weeks old: «a newborn baby», «a newborn lamb».
explain: Newborn can be an adjective, which describes a thing: «a newborn lamb» tells you which lamb. It can also be a noun, a baby that has just been born. Newborns is the plural.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «Marsupials... carry their tiny newborns in a pouch.» Tiny and pouch tell you that newborns are very small and very young. Swap in just born and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Newborn means just born, only a few hours, days or weeks old.
fact: As an adjective, newborn describes a noun: «a newborn baby», «a newborn lamb».
fact: As a noun, a newborn is a baby that has just been born, and newborns is the plural.
fact: «Newborn babies can suck, cry and grip, but walking and talking are learned slowly.»
fact: Newborn animals need milk and care from their parents, and some, like foals, can walk within hours.
exercise: «Marsupials, such as kangaroos and koalas, carry their tiny newborns in a pouch.» What does newborns mean here? | Adult animals that have grown very big | Animals with no legs | *Babies that have just been born | Animals that live under water
exercise: «Newborn babies can suck, cry and grip, but walking and talking are learned slowly.» Which of these can a newborn baby do? | Read a book | Walk and talk well | *Suck, cry and grip | Drive a car
exercise: Which phrase means a baby that has just been born? | *a newborn baby | a lost baby | a grown-up baby | a sleepy teacher
test: «A newborn blue whale can gain about 90 kilograms a day.» What does newborn tell you about the whale? | It is a fish with no tail | *It is very young, just born | It is swimming away from its mother | It is very old and large
test: «Babies start learning language before birth; newborns prefer their mother's voice.» What does newborns mean in this sentence? | Animals that cannot hear | *Babies that have just been born | Mothers who have just had a baby | Adults who are learning to talk
exam: Which sentence uses newborn as an adjective? | The newborn was asleep in the cot. | Many newborns hear their mother's voice before birth. | *The newborn lamb stood up on its wobbly legs. | Newborns need milk and care from their parents.
